  "Question": "A taxi ride costs \\(\\$1.50\\) plus \\(\\$0.25\\) per mile traveled. How much does a \\(5\\)-mile taxi ride cost?",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(\\$2.25\\)",
    "B": "\\(\\$2.50\\)",
    "C": "\\(\\$2.75\\)",
    "D": "\\(\\$3.00\\)",
    "E": "\\(\\$3.25\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "C",
  "Solution": "The fare has a fixed charge of \\(\\$1.50\\) and a mileage charge of \\(\\$0.25\\) for each of the five miles. Therefore the total cost is\n\\[\n\\$1.50+5(\\$0.25)\n=\\$1.50+\\$1.25\n=\\boxed{\\$2.75}.\n\\]\nThe answer is C.",
